start                      : stack = [X soup, Y rice, Z tea]
A reads top = X soup, next = Y rice, then pauses
B popped X                 : stack = [Y rice, Z tea]
B popped Y and reused it   : stack = [Z tea]
B pushed X back            : stack = [X soup, Z tea]
A's CAS(top: X -> Y reused: bread, table 9) SUCCEEDED
after A's pop              : stack = [Y reused: bread, table 9]
A returns X soup. The correct result was [Z tea]: instead the stack holds a node B had already taken, and Z tea is lost
